# Contributing

Thank you for having an interest in contributing.
This is very unnecessary, as this is a personal config.
But feel free to.

## Code of Conduct:

See the `CODE_OF_CONDUCT` in the root. It's a simple read.

## How to Contribute:

### Bug Reports

Check the issues, if it is already there don't worry about it.
If it isn't there, feel free to make it.
Just include everything you can: Host name, nix version, error logs, steps on how it happened, whatever else.
Or just contact me personally the contact info is in my GitHub readme.

### Pull Requests

If you decided to use this for some reason, feel free to.
Although I think you should make your own personal nix config.

I highly recommend reading the NixOS wiki or the following YouTubers:

- Vimjoyer
- Ampersand
- Finley
- Tony

Cool guys.

I am also willing to respond to any questions if anyone has any regarding Nix (if I can answer, that is).
GitHub issues, Instagram, Email, wherever else.

If you decide to use this still, I'd recommend just forking the repo for yourself.
And having a personal setup based on this.

If you really want to partake in this for whatever reason.
Just fork the repo.
And make a branch and then do a PR upstream if you want.
Please add to `tests/` if you can.
Please do not make any breaking changes I will be very sad if you do.
Make PRs clear because I'm very busy and will not go through all of that.

